9,"Native American music - Mexico, Central America, Rituals | Britannica",https://www.britannica.com/art/Native-American-music/Mexico-and-Central-America,"November 20, 2007 - Part-singing and call and response continue to play a role in religious songs from Central Mexico, and instrumental ensembles employ chordal harmony. Dance music from this area features sectional forms with several short musical phrases in succession. The Mixtec perform certain song genres in their native languages, while other Central Mexican groups sing in Spanish.","Mixtec, Metlatónoc",Otomanguean
